  - processor grid for Pi: (w, q, P, Q) = (1, 2, 1, 1)
  - block size: (w, q, P, Q) = (1, 1, 128, 128)
  RPA spectrum: max 1/n_eff = |resid|/(Tr^2/2) = 5.7565e-02 at iq=7 iw=54 (Tr there -1.149878e-01, resid -3.805647e-04). This is the inverse participation ratio of Pi*Z -- small = weight spread over many modes, ~1 = a single mode carries the block. Only blocks with |Tr| above a floor are eligible -- an empty high-frequency block otherwise returns a garbage O(1) ratio from noise/noise^2. Proximity to the ln(1-lambda) singularity is a DIFFERENT question, tested exactly by the log_det<0 / Tr>0 warning.
  RPA term split: Tr(Pi*Z) = -1.54828025, ln|det(I-Pi*Z)| = 1.31328805, sum = -0.23499219 Ha. The two are individually large and opposite in sign; E_c is what survives their cancellation, so comparing the split across runs localizes a change that E_c alone hides.

